Z||000006||rogergarrison||04-21-2001||06:59 AM||||we tried this same thing last summer but target was British Petroleum (AKA BP)it may or may not have had any effect, no figures were ever released. A better idea was no matter what brand of gas you use, dont buy anything at stations but gas. Most make more profit from other products and services. Itll hurt them more in the pocketbook, with no big inconvenience to you. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||hugh||04-21-2001||07:48 AM||||Roger,Quite a few stations are run or owned by individuals who pay rent and buy their gas from the oil companies.It is bad enough that they have to meet quotas competing against company owned stations.If you stopped using them for repairs and other purchases like tires or whatever,you wouldn't hurt the oil company,you would hurt the little guy in the middle(sort of like kill the messanger).I think the company owned stores would be the best targets for a gas boycott.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||04-21-2001||08:01 AM||||true hugh.....but if the owners knew WHY you werent buying anything else. THEYD be doing the griping to the oil companies. It would be in the oil companies interest to listen since if the station went out of business-theyd lose a customer too. I dont even buy a can of pop. When they say 'is there anything else I just tell em 'no, ill buy it down the street because the gas is to high'. And yes I agree, company owned stations would be the best, they sell lots of other stuff too.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||MontanaFiero||04-21-2001||01:24 PM||||just find out which stations in your community <I>are</I> company owned (by oil companies) and don't buy anything there. Make sure you buy your gas at independent stores or independent chains (that don't have ExxonMobil as their supplier)<P>Oh, and Roger, Do you really think that the  minimum wage counterperson is actually going to run to his manager or the store owner/operator and tell them "you said the price is too high so your buying your pop somewhere else?" I don't think the message will get through.||||reg||1
