Z||000012||Raydar||04-23-2001||03:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MontanaFiero:<BR><B>just find out which stations in your community <I>are</I> company owned (by oil companies) and don't buy anything there. Make sure you buy your gas at independent stores or independent chains (that don't have ExxonMobil as their supplier)<P>Oh, and Roger, Do you really think that the  minimum wage counterperson is actually going to run to his manager or the store owner/operator and tell them "you said the price is too high so your buying your pop somewhere else?" I don't think the message will get through.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My in-laws used to own a "mom 'n' pop" convenience store. They had no say-so when it came to the oil companies. The oil companies pretty much told <I>them</I> what to do. Not to mention all the environmental crap they had to put up with just to have gas on the premesis. So DON'T boycott the little folks. The oil companies would LOVE to see them fold. That way, they could be "annexed" into the company store.<BR>I try to NOT buy gas at an Exxon station if there is an alternative available. <BR>BTW... Anyone know where Quik Trip buys their gas?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Black88GT||04-23-2001||03:30 PM||||I heard that the smaller "mom and pop" gas stations were getting run out of town by these big oil companies since they can't afford to buy the gas from them and make a profit since Exxon across the street can sell it cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000014||DRH||04-23-2001||03:55 PM||||Here's an article about what big oil is doing to the mom and pop stations. Sounds like an excuse to eliminate competition to me...<BR> <A HREF="http://news.moneycentral.msn.com/ticker/article.asp?Symbol=US:XOM&Feed=RTR&Date=20010418&ID=699941" TARGET=_blank>http://news.moneycentral.msn.com/ticker/article.asp?Symbol=US:XOM&Feed=RTR&Date=20010418&ID=699941</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||09:32 AM||||I sorta ran a 'mom n pop' thing myself. I managed a county airport in ohio about 10 years ago. I purchased avgas from a large airport for around 60 cents @ gallon. The norm rate at the time for customers at the pump was about $1.75 @ gal. Some of the based owners complained about the high gas cost and I dropped my prices by .25 and still made money and everyone was happy. Even planes from other airports would stop in route or even make special trips just to fill up at ours. So bitching can make a difference. Im still all for the going after oil company stations over the mom-n-pops but you gotta do what you can do.||||reg||1
